168: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
169: 
170: ### Constraints
171: - Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, routes, 
and query keys rather than parallel implementations.
172: - Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages link 
to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
173: - Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated E2E); Firefox desktop (verified). Safari and mobile not required.
174: - No service worker; background notifications are page-level only.
175: - No message text, names, or identifiers in metrics (BR-013); no external analytics service.
176: - The sign-out confirmation must not change the Presence logout sequence (presence-safety rules apply to that 
touch point).
177: - Online database changes only at phase end with explicit authorization (BR-014); the hosted app currently runs 
the pre-Phase-4 build until the owner deploys, so new server contracts must stay compatible with that build and with 
the Phase 4 build until deployment: unkeyed legacy message writes and existing RPC/route signatures keep working 
against the migrated database.
178: - Repository test policy (BR-015); type-check, lint, and build must pass.
179: - Timing parameters chosen under the owner's delegation (D4) and adjustable in planning only with owner approval: 
claim request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s, metrics batch ≤ 50 events / 16 KB, one metrics delivery in flight, 5 s metrics 
abort.
180: 
181: ### Assumptions
182: - None beyond the user-confirmed answers and owner decisions recorded in `state.md`.
183: 
184: ## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
185: 
186: | Case | Expected behavior |
187: |---|---|
188: | Tab closed right after pressing send, before server confirmation | Item is already in the outbox; on next load 
it is fenced and delivered once (AC-040). |
189: | Request stored but response lost | Item becomes unknown; fence finds it stored; resolves as delivered; never 
offered for cancel or expired (AC-038, AC-042). |
190: | Original create blocked before its INSERT, or still in the network, while another tab fences | The fence wins; 
the older generation can no longer commit; the item is resent once or cancelled/expired without a late duplicate 
(AC-045). |
191: | Stale fence arrives after a takeover | Rejected as an older generation; the newer attempt is unaffected 
(AC-045). |
192: | Hung holder when connectivity returns | Its attempt is superseded at once; D1 deadline holds (AC-041). |
193: | Two tabs come online together | One drain claim per conversation; only the oldest unresolved item is eligible; 
no overlapping create requests for that conversation; each stored and shown once, in order (AC-005). |
194: | Owning tab closes or hangs mid-request | Closed or lease expired: another tab fences and finishes once; while 
the lease is live no other tab dispatches (AC-041). |
195: | Cancel races a claim | Exactly one wins; a cancelled item is never dispatched; a dispatched item cannot be 
cancelled (AC-006). |
196: | Lost access before reconnect | First item fails definitively with text; later items of that conversation wait; 
other conversations deliver (AC-007). |
197: | Access regained after failure | "Tentar de novo" delivers it, then the waiting items in order (AC-008). |
198: | Other definitive outcomes (404, 400, 413, 422) and 5xx | Definitive → failed with text; 5xx → unknown → fence 
(AC-046). |
199: | `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` | Failed; "Tentar de novo" resends the content under a new key, once (AC-043). |
200: | Server rate limit during drain; concurrent same-key requests | Items stay pending, retried automatically; quota 
charged once per stored message; replays/fences use a separate budget (AC-009). |
201: | Laptop asleep > 24 h | Not-stored items become "expirada"; stored ones resolve as delivered (AC-010, AC-042). |
202: | Offline attachment / voice | Upload failure: per-file error + retry; create failure after upload: Phase 4 
composer failure; nothing in the outbox (AC-011). |
203: | IndexedDB unavailable or write fails | Nothing dispatched; text stays in the composer with the storage message 
(D5) (AC-039). |
204: | Identical texts sent twice; Realtime arrives before the HTTP response | One bubble per message, matched by key 
(AC-050). |
205: | Account switched while a drain is paused or a response is in flight | Drain stops; no dispatch as the new user; 
late responses discarded; server rejects any request whose sender differs (AC-044, AC-047). |
206: | Session ends without Sair; other user signs in | Other user never sees/sends A's items; A's items drain after A 
signs in (AC-012). |
207: | Temporary Auth failure (401 with valid client session) | Treated as transient; retried; not held or deleted 
(AC-012). |
208: | Sair with unsent items | Dialog; Cancelar has no side effects at any entry point; Sair mesmo stops drains 
everywhere and deletes the outbox; late responses do not resurrect items (AC-013, AC-047). |
209: | Realtime drop < 5 s | No "Reconectando…" banner (AC-014). |
210: | Only the conversation-list stream fails | Banner after 5 s and polling after 30 s follow its health; recovered 
independently (AC-015, AC-016). |
211: | Stale poll returns after a newer Realtime update | Newer/enriched state kept; no duplicates (AC-048). |

