State delta:
- On the LOCAL database (migration `supabase/migrations/20261007114454_message_create_budgets_insert_quota.sql`, 
written + applied locally, revised in place twice (r1, r2) with header rollback + reapply each time, NOT online): the 
insertion quota ('message:create', 30/60 s) is charged by `private.charge_message_insertion_quota` (SECURITY DEFINER, 
search_path '', service_role only) as the last step of a winning insertion inside `public.create_message_attempt` (now 
11 arguments: + `p_insert_quota_limit`, `p_insert_quota_window_seconds`): per-user lock held to commit, window read 
from the clock after the lock, then older windows deleted. Replays, lost same-key races and refused creates are never 
charged; RATE_LIMITED / RATE_LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE roll back the insertion and its attachment links.
- `public.check_rate_limit` redefined: action 'message:create' delegates to the same quota helper (a Phase 4 server's 
route charge is serialized with T3 insertions; INSERT_QUOTA_INVALID 22023 on invalid limit/window); every other action 
keeps the 20260612190000 body verbatim.
- Direct client inserts removed: policy "send_message_as_self" dropped and INSERT on public.messages revoked from 
anon/authenticated (git history: no browser build inserts messages; only server routes, all service-role since 
2026-02-23).
- Unkeyed creates go through `create_message_attempt` (null key/generation) via `createUnkeyed`; the function returns 
the created row (`INSERT … RETURNING`, `message` key) built in the insertion transaction and mapped directly (no 
post-commit readback; fallback read only if the row were malformed). The Phase 4 wrapper 
`create_message_with_attachments` strips `message` and `composition` (its `{message_id, created}` result is unchanged).
- Only the exact 'NOT_PARTICIPANT' marker (42501) maps to 403; any other 42501 (revoked grants) → 500; budget failures 
→ 429.
- Routes: `POST /api/messages/create` authenticates, then charges 'message:create-request' (60/60 s) in its own 
transaction before parsing the body (malformed, validation failures, replays, quota losers all charged; survives 
insertion rollback; 401 charges nobody). `POST /api/messages/fence` charges 'message:fence' (90/60 s, was 60; the T2 
fail-open limiter is replaced) on every authenticated call; the fence step of a generation-carrying create charges it 
too. These three budgets fail closed (RPC error, revoked/missing function, non-boolean → 429); 
react/upload/upload-cancel/read-receipts keep their fail-open limits.
- Budgets:

  | Budget | Limit | Charged by |
  |---|---|---|
  | `message:create` (insertion quota) | 30/60 s | winning insertion only, in the DB transaction (+ Phase 4 route 
charges, serialized) |
